# component-dataflow

Core Data Flow Components:

1. Psychology Engine → Intervention Engine
Paths: backend/app/services/psychology_engine.py → backend/app/services/intervention_engine.py
- Transmits trauma impact calculations and developmental stage data
- Forwards symptom assessments for intervention matching
- Passes personality trait modifications based on therapeutic progress
- Streams real-time psychological state updates
Importance Score: 95

2. Developmental Stages System → Symptom Assessment
Paths: backend/app/utils/developmental_stages.py → backend/app/utils/symptom_assessment_engine.py
- Maps age-based vulnerabilities to disorder risk calculations
- Provides developmental context for symptom severity scoring
- Transmits stage-appropriate coping capacity metrics
Importance Score: 90

3. Backstory Analysis → Symptom Taxonomy 
Paths: backend/app/utils/backstory_symptom_mapper.py → backend/app/utils/symptom_taxonomy.py
- Feeds trauma markers into disorder classification system
- Maps early life experiences to potential symptom manifestations
- Streams severity scores for diagnostic categorization
Importance Score: 85

4. Clinical Templates → Therapy Efficacy System
Paths: frontend/components/templates/TemplateDetailsModal.tsx → backend/app/utils/therapy_database.py
- Transmits evidence-based treatment patterns
- Forwards therapy matching criteria
- Streams outcome measurement data
Importance Score: 80

Key Integration Points:
- Psychology Engine serves as central hub for state management
- Intervention Engine provides feedback loops to update psychological models
- Developmental data flows inform all assessment and treatment decisions
- Bidirectional flows between analysis and intervention components maintain therapeutic consistency

